{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"1. **Additional refactoring strategy used**  \nSelected responsibility: **DOM tree mutation/building** in `Element` (child insertion, prepend/append APIs, wrapping/emptying).  \nI extracted that responsibility into a focused collaborator superclass `ElementTreeOps`, and made `Element` inherit it, so public API remains available through inheritance while reducing methods directly implemented in `Element`.\n\n2. **Files changed**  \n- Added [ElementTreeOps.java](/data/henrique/langchain_prototype/codex/data/repositories/jsoup/src/main/java/org/jsoup/nodes/ElementTreeOps.java:1)  \n- Updated [Element.java](/data/henrique/langchain_prototype/codex/data/repositories/jsoup/src/main/java/org/jsoup/nodes/Element.java:37)\n\n3. **Expected impact on the smell**  \n- Moved/extracted methods (21 total) from `Element` into `ElementTreeOps`:  \n`appendChild`, `appendChildren`, `appendTo`, `prependChild`, `prependChildren`, both `insertChildren` overloads, both `appendElement` overloads, both `prependElement` overloads, `appendText`, `prependText`, `append`, `prepend`, `before(String)`, `before(Node)`, `after(String)`, `after(Node)`, `empty`, `wrap`.  \n- `Element` is simplified by delegating this cohesive structural-editing responsibility to the extracted collaborator, which should materially reduce `Element`’s method counts toward Designite IM thresholds.\n\n4. **Validation command executed**  \nExecuted:  \n`mvn -q -Djapicmp.skip=true -Drat.skip=true -Dcheckstyle.skip=true -Dspotbugs.skip=true -Dpmd.skip=true -DskipITs clean verify`  \nResult: failed due to sandbox network/socket restrictions in Netty-backed integration tests (`Operation not permitted`), not due to compilation errors.  \nAlso ran: `mvn -q -DskipTests compile` → passed.\n\n5. **Remaining risks**  \n- I could not run a fully passing `clean verify` in this environment because tests requiring local socket binding fail here.  \n- Designite was not re-run in this environment, so smell removal is inferred from method relocation and class simplification."}}
